{#
  The webmaster's note, top or bottom.

  It was a cream strip with a gold left rule and no heading, which read as a
  pull quote or as part of the prose depending on where it fell. It is now the
  same box as record/editor-notes.twig: cream ground, thin border, 3px gold top
  rule, a small caps label above the text. Both are the archive speaking about
  the piece rather than the author speaking in it, so they should look alike.

  The label is "Note:" unless the caller passes another, and a record can
  override it without a schema change by opening the note with a short line of
  its own ending in a colon:

      Webmaster's note:
      The dates on this page come from the family Bible rather than the census.

  That first line becomes the label and is not printed twice. It has to be
  short, on its own line and colon-terminated, so a note that simply begins
  "In 1887: the depot opened" is left alone. Nothing in the corpus uses the
  convention today, 69 of the 70 notes having no leading label at all; it is
  here so a per-record label does not need a new field.

  The handle differs by entry type, so the caller passes the value rather than
  this partial guessing: webmasterNoteTop / webmasterNoteBottom on most types,
  personWebmasterNote* on People, obitWebmasterNote* on Obituaries and
  mpWebmasterNote* on Military Profiles.

  Params:
    text    the note, plain text or simple HTML
    bottom  true for the note under the piece
    label   overrides the default, and is itself overridden by a label in the text
#}
{% if text is defined and text is not empty and text|trim %}
  {%- set raw = text|trim -%}
  {%- set lines = raw|split("\n") -%}
  {%- set firstLine = lines|first|trim -%}

  {#- A label line, not a sentence that happens to contain a colon. Short, on
      its own line, ending in the colon, and with no colon before the end. -#}
  {%- set isLabelLine = lines|length > 1
        and firstLine|length > 1 and firstLine|length <= 40
        and firstLine|slice(-1) == ':'
        and firstLine|slice(0, -1)|split(':')|length == 1 -%}

  {%- set lab = isLabelLine ? firstLine|slice(0, -1)|trim : (label|default('Note'))|trim|trim(':') -%}
  {%- set bodyText = isLabelLine ? lines|slice(1)|join("\n")|trim : raw -%}

  {% css %}
  .rec-note{background:#FDF7EA;border:1px solid #EFE6D0;border-top:3px solid #C4A031;padding:16px 20px;margin:0 0 28px}
  .rec-note:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .rec-note .h{font-family:'Jost',sans-serif;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7A5C1B;margin:0 0 8px}
  .rec-note .t{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#2C2C2C}
  .rec-note .t p{margin:0 0 12px}
  .rec-note .t p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .rec-note .t a{color:#7A5C1B}
  .rec-note--bottom{margin:36px 0 0}
  {% endcss %}
  <div class="rec-note{{ bottom is defined and bottom ? ' rec-note--bottom' : '' }}">
    <div class="h">{{ lab }}</div>
    <div class="t">{{ bodyText|raw }}</div>
  </div>
{% endif %}
